  "content": {
    "id": "p45-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Write down the radius of each circle or semicircle. Also state any points on each curve whose coordinates are both integers.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 4,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p45-q17-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2+y^2=5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\sqrt5$; $(\\pm1,\\pm2)$ and $(\\pm2,\\pm1)$, with independent signs.",
          "worked": "$r^2=5$, so $r=\\sqrt5$. The only integer-square decomposition is $5=1+4$.\n\nHence the points are $(1,2)$, $(1,-2)$, $(-1,2)$, $(-1,-2)$, $(2,1)$, $(2,-1)$, $(-2,1)$ and $(-2,-1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q17-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=-\\sqrt{2-x^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\sqrt2$; $(1,-1)$ and $(-1,-1)$.",
          "worked": "Squaring gives $x^2+y^2=2$, with $y\\leq0$.\n\nThus $r=\\sqrt2$. Since $2=1+1$, the integer points on the lower semicircle are $(1,-1)$ and $(-1,-1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q17-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x=\\sqrt{10-y^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\sqrt{10}$; $(3,1)$, $(3,-1)$, $(1,3)$ and $(1,-3)$.",
          "worked": "Squaring gives $x^2+y^2=10$, with $x\\geq0$.\n\nThus $r=\\sqrt{10}$. Since $10=1+9$, the integer points on the right semicircle are $(3,1)$, $(3,-1)$, $(1,3)$ and $(1,-3)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q17-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^2+y^2=17$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\sqrt{17}$; $(\\pm1,\\pm4)$ and $(\\pm4,\\pm1)$, with independent signs.",
          "worked": "$r^2=17$, so $r=\\sqrt{17}$. The only integer-square decomposition is $17=1+16$.\n\nHence the points are $(1,4)$, $(1,-4)$, $(-1,4)$, $(-1,-4)$, $(4,1)$, $(4,-1)$, $(-4,1)$ and $(-4,-1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
